==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/haiː/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|aiː|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|is|en|hi}} some time after 1970, possibly also influenced by Danish {{m|da|hej}}.

====Interjection====
{{head|is|interjection}}

# {{lb|is|informal}} [[hi]]
#: {{syn|is|halló}}

=====Usage notes=====
{{m|is|hæ|Hæ}} is a relatively informal greeting, but very common. The greetings {{m|is|sæll}}, {{m|is|blessaður}}, {{m|is|góðan dag}} and {{m|is|gótt kvöld}}/{{m|is|gótt kveld}} are more appropriate in formal situations.

The use of {{m|is|hæ}} and {{m|is|bæ}} (corresponding to English {{m|en|hi}} and {{m|en|bye}}) was frowned upon by older speakers well into the 2000s.

===Etymology 2===

====Interjection====
{{head|is|interjection}}

# [[hey]]! {{gloss|an exclamation to get attention}}
# {{l|en|ha}}!, {{l|en|yippee}}! {{gloss|an exclamation of [[joy]]}}
#: {{uxi|is|Hæ, hæ og hó, hó! [[húsfreyja|Húsfreyja]] veit {{l|is|ei}} hvað ég heiti! [[Gilitrutt]] heit ég!|Yippee! The lady does not know my name. [[Gilitrutt]] is my name!}}

